    pr_ref:  # b81f
    justification:  # b81f
    description: "Cross-cutting invariant. DSL references (router configs, GenServer targets, ORM model names) frequently use aliased or short names. Known violations: (1) OTP linker — direct dict lookup, no suffix fallback, HIGH severity. (2) Phoenix route_handler — suffix scan fails on alias...as: patterns, MEDIUM. (3) Laravel route_handler — no suffix-match fallback unlike Rails, MEDIUM. (4) Django route_handler — only 2-level fallback, LOW. Structural pattern: any linker resolving string references needs at minimum exact match, suffix match, and alias-aware resolution. Rails route_handler 5-tier cascade is the gold standard."  # b81f
    fields:  # b81f
      statement: "Linkers that resolve references from DSL syntax must handle aliased/short names that don't match fully-qualified symbol names in the graph"  # b81f
      root_cause: "Multiple linkers use direct dict lookup or insufficient fallback when DSL references use module aliases or namespace shortcuts"  # b81f
